    "updated_at": "2023-09-18T16:58:35Z",
    "body": "> The pseudo-class matches all elements that do not match `:read-write`: https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#selector-read-only. And so yes, that includes elements to which the `readonly` attribute does not apply. That seems orthogonal to this issue.\r\n\r\n\"The pseudo-class matches all elements that do not match `:read-write`.\" \r\n\r\nYes, that is my point, `read-only` is not an accurate descriptor. Because it is, in functional practice, \"not read-write.\" I think the text should be changed.",
